<!DOCTYPE html>
<html data-surface="studio" lang="en">
  <head>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) || t("admin.layout.product.title") %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>
    <%# turbo-rails' consumer reads the socket's address here and otherwise asks /cable. %>
    <%= action_cable_meta_tag %>
    <%= render "shared/theme_head" %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag "tailwind", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
    <%# The `application` entry point, or CS Studio's (`admin`) for a page
        that asks with `content_for :entry_point` (enrolment, which draws
        the Passkeys card's script and Confirm it's you). %>
    <%= javascript_importmap_tags(content_for(:entry_point) == "admin" ? "admin" : "application") %>
    <%# A page's own head lines (sign-in's `turbo-visit-control`). %>
    <%= yield :head %>
  </head>

  <%# Product UI layout for sign-in, the password reset, an invitation and
      passkey enrolment:
      product stylesheet, no public header/footer. The header is the
      wordmark (a link home to sign-in) and the theme switch, with no rule
      under it. Below it, in a centred 420px column, the page stands on one
      panel: `surface` at elevation 2 (`shadow-2`), `rounded-rail`, 24px of
      padding (`p-6`) below 480px and 32px (`p-8`) from there. The words are read by
      full key (`admin.layout.product.*`): a lazy lookup from a layout lands
      in `layouts.product.*`.
      color-scheme stays scoped to this body. %>
  <body class="min-h-screen bg-paper font-cs text-ink scheme-light dark:scheme-dark">
    <header class="flex items-center justify-between px-7 py-5">
      <%= render "admin/shared/product_wordmark" %>
      <%= render Admin::Ui::ThemeSwitchComponent.new %>
    </header>
    <main class="px-[22px] pb-16 pt-16">
      <%# A password is typed on every page of this layout (sign-in, the
          reset request, the new password and an invitation), so the notice
          that the connection is plain HTTP is here once, for everyone,
          above the panel: nobody is signed in yet. Production only (the
          component's own rule). %>
      <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[420px]">
        <%= render Admin::Ui::InsecureNoticeComponent.new(request: request, class: "mb-[18px]") %>
        <div class="rounded-rail bg-surface p-6 shadow-2 min-[480px]:p-8">
          <%= yield %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
